  "sections": [
    [
      "Four priority watersheds",
      [
        "The four original RFP focus HUC12s retain 53,008.20 hectares of paired-valid source support. 1,580.85 hectares change annual classification (2.9823%). Their developed-group balance is +251.28 ha; forest balance is -233.73 ha.",
        "Lower Six And Twenty contributes 125.73 ha of that developed-group net increase. Its original matrix specifically records 48.96 ha moving from forest classes to developed classes and 53.55 ha from agriculture classes to developed classes. These directional crossings are components of the complete balance, not the net balance itself.",
